From 083e4bcc81ac509de285561fcc20d531b8f43b55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 20:17:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add light/dark theme system

- Enable Tailwind class-based dark mode (darkMode: 'class')
- Add ThemeContext/ThemeProvider: reads localStorage first, falls
  back to OS preference (prefers-color-scheme), keeps following the
  OS live until the user explicitly toggles, and persists the choice
- Add anti-flash inline script in public/index.html that sets the
  dark class before first paint (no light-then-dark flicker)
- Add ThemeToggle sun/moon button, wired into Navbar desktop + mobile
- Add dark: variants to Navbar links and mobile menu panel
- Add base html/body dark background + text color with a smooth
  color-scheme transition in index.css

This is the foundation layer only: Navbar, mobile menu, and global
body background/text now respond correctly to the toggle. Per-page
component styling (Home, About, Services, etc.) will get dark:
variants in a follow-up pass.
